.TH FATHOM_DAEMON 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-daemon \- The one process per repository that watches, tails the harness stream and indexes (`e6.3`)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom daemon\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The one process per repository that watches, tails the harness stream and indexes (`e6.3`)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
fathom\-daemon\-start(1)
Take the writer lease and watch this repository from this process, or from a detached one
.TP
fathom\-daemon\-stop(1)
Ask the daemon to finish its pass, checkpoint and release the lease
.TP
fathom\-daemon\-status(1)
The daemon\*(Aqs own health report (`fathom status` is the same question at the top level)
